<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  AnimalDessicatedTexPaths_Fix.xml           Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-21
  ============================================================================

  Six dead `dessicatedBodyGraphicData/texPath` strings across three animal
  mods, all found by jawa/texture_audit against the LIVE process on the full
  mod list (first_light_2026-08-21_0123.md). GRiNDTerra's equivalents live in
  `GrimTerraTexPaths_Fix.xml`; this file is everything else.

  🪤 EVERY ONE OF THESE IS ON A PawnKindDef, NOT ON THE ANIMAL'S ThingDef.
  The ThingDef carries race/lifeStages with `dessicatedTexPath`; these sit on
  the PAWNKIND's own lifeStages under `dessicatedBodyGraphicData/texPath` -
  a different node, on a different def, with the same-looking shape. An xpath
  aimed at the ThingDef matches nothing, and a PatchOperation that matches
  nothing logs nothing, so it would have looked exactly like a fix.

  🔑 A DESSICATED texPath IS THE LAST THING ANYONE NOTICES. It is only read
  when a corpse finishes rotting, so none of these appears in a load harvest
  and none of them breaks the living animal. They are found by auditing the
  content index, not by playing.

  ⚠️ Case is compared character by character below. Windows' filesystem is
  case-insensitive and RimWorld's content index is NOT, so a path can resolve
  from a shell and still fail in game. Never settle one of these with `ls`.

  =========================================================================
  Biomes! Caverns (workshop 2969748433) - verified against its Textures tree
  =========================================================================
    is    Things/Pawn/Animal/BeardedYak/Dessicated_BeardedYak
    want  BMT_Caverns/Things/Animal/BeardedYak/Dessicated_BeardedYak
          Mod prefix dropped. The path as written points into VANILLA's
          Things/Pawn/Animal/, where no bearded yak has ever existed. Its own
          `bodyGraphicData` two lines above carries the BMT_Caverns prefix
          correctly, which is what makes this a slip rather than a design.

    is    BMT_Caverns/Things/Animal/FreezerFrog/Dessicated_FreezerFrog
    want  BMT_Caverns/Things/Animal/FreezerFrog/Dessicated_FreezertFrog
          The FILE is the misspelt one - `FreezertFrog`, with a stray t - and
          the def is right. We cannot rename art in a workshop folder, so the
          patch bends the def to the file.
          ⚠️ ONE LOOSE END, RECORDED RATHER THAN GUESSED AT. The file also
          has no directional suffix: its Caverns siblings ship
          `Dessicated_*_east.png` and this ships a bare
          `Dessicated_FreezertFrog.png`, while Graphic_Multi looks for
          _north/_east/_south/_west. That is probably fine - every dessicated
          sprite in Star Wars Animal Collection is suffixless too and none of
          those was flagged - but it is untested, and if the frog corpse still
          fails to draw after this patch, the suffix is where to look. Either
          way it would be a defect in the mod's ART, not in its path.

    is    Things/Pawn/Animal/GlarralPenguin/Dessicated_GlarralPenguin
    want  BMT_Caverns/Things/Animal/GlarralPenguin/Dessicated_GlarralPenguin
          Same dropped prefix as the yak, same file, same author.

  All three animals declare THREE identical lifeStages, so each op below
  matches three nodes, not one. PatchOperationReplace replaces every match.

  =========================================================================
  Star Wars Animal Collection (Continued) (workshop 3497316713)
  =========================================================================
  🔑 THIS MOD SHIPS NO LOOSE PNGs. Its `Textures/` folder holds only
  UpdateInfo; the art is inside `AssetBundles/Mlie_StarWarsAnimalCollection`,
  and the authority on what exists is the `.manifest` beside it. Anyone who
  concludes "the texture is missing" from a `find` over Textures/ is wrong
  about every animal in the mod.

    is    swanimals/Bursa_Dessicated
    want  swanimals/Bursa/Bursa_Dessicated
          Folder segment dropped. Its own lifeStages[1] and [2] already read
          the correct form; only the BABY stage is broken.

    is    swanimals/KGreaterKraytDragon/GreaterKraytDragon_Dessicated
    want  swanimals/GreaterKraytDragon/GreaterKraytDragon_Dessicated
          A stray leading K on the folder. Again only lifeStages[0].

  ⛔ NOT FIXED, AND NOT FIXABLE HERE: Yobshrimp lifeStages[0] wants
  `swanimals/Yobshrimp/Yobshrimp_j_Dessicated`. The bundle holds
  Yobshrimp_j_east/_north/_south and Yobshrimp_Dessicated, but there is no
  juvenile dessicated sprite at all - the art was never drawn. (KraytDragon,
  by contrast, does ship a _j_Dessicated, which is how we know the convention
  is real and this is an omission.) Pointing it at the ADULT
  `swanimals/Yobshrimp/Yobshrimp_Dessicated` would silence the error at the
  cost of substituting art the author did not choose; that is an owner call,
  not a typo repair, so it is left alone and reported instead.

  =========================================================================
  Insectoids 2 - Isopoda geneline (workshop 3357632382)
  =========================================================================
    is    Things/Pawn/Animal/SW_GrenadeBug/SW_Dessicated_EngineerBug
    want  Things/Pawn/Animal/SW_GrenadeBug/SW_Dessicated_GrenadeBug
          Half of a copy-paste: the FOLDER was updated to SW_GrenadeBug and
          the FILENAME was not. Both `SW_EngineerBug/SW_Dessicated_EngineerBug`
          and `SW_GrenadeBug/SW_Dessicated_GrenadeBug` exist, so the pair
          could be reconciled in either direction - we take the GrenadeBug
          one because the electrictick's LIVING sprite is
          `SW_GrenadeBug/SW_GrenadeBug`, and a corpse should look like the
          thing that died.

  =========================================================================
  Each operation targets the node BY ITS CURRENT VALUE rather than by
  position. li[1] would be correct today and wrong the moment anything inserts
  a life stage; a value predicate cannot drift, because only the broken node
  carries the broken string.

  🪤 THE PREDICATE GOES ON THE PARENT, NOT ON THE texPath ITSELF. The obvious
  form, texPath[.="..."], is XPath 1.0 and RimWorld would accept it - but the
  offline validator walks the defs with ElementTree, which does not implement
  a self-predicate and reports 0 matches. The form below,
  dessicatedBodyGraphicData[texPath="..."]/texPath, is a CHILD-VALUE predicate
  and is the house form both engines agree on.

  ⛔ DO NOT EDIT THE WORKSHOP FOLDERS. Steam overwrites them on update.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Biomes! Caverns</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="BMT_BeardedYak"]/lifeStages/li/dessicatedBodyGraphicData[texPath="Things/Pawn/Animal/BeardedYak/Dessicated_BeardedYak"]/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>BMT_Caverns/Things/Animal/BeardedYak/Dessicated_BeardedYak</texPath></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="BMT_FreezerFrog"]/lifeStages/li/dessicatedBodyGraphicData[texPath="BMT_Caverns/Things/Animal/FreezerFrog/Dessicated_FreezerFrog"]/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>BMT_Caverns/Things/Animal/FreezerFrog/Dessicated_FreezertFrog</texPath></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="BMT_GlarralPenguin"]/lifeStages/li/dessicatedBodyGraphicData[texPath="Things/Pawn/Animal/GlarralPenguin/Dessicated_GlarralPenguin"]/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>BMT_Caverns/Things/Animal/GlarralPenguin/Dessicated_GlarralPenguin</texPath></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Star Wars Animal Collection (Continued)</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Bursa"]/lifeStages/li/dessicatedBodyGraphicData[texPath="swanimals/Bursa_Dessicated"]/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>swanimals/Bursa/Bursa_Dessicated</texPath></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="GreaterKraytDragon"]/lifeStages/li/dessicatedBodyGraphicData[texPath="swanimals/KGreaterKraytDragon/GreaterKraytDragon_Dessicated"]/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>swanimals/GreaterKraytDragon/GreaterKraytDragon_Dessicated</texPath></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Insectoids 2 - Isopoda geneline</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="SW_Electrictick"]/lifeStages/li/dessicatedBodyGraphicData[texPath="Things/Pawn/Animal/SW_GrenadeBug/SW_Dessicated_EngineerBug"]/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/SW_GrenadeBug/SW_Dessicated_GrenadeBug</texPath></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
